  "summary": "An explainer from the Dayton Daily News/Journal-News describes how Flock and other ALPR systems work, how southwest Ohio police share data, and concerns raised by privacy advocates and a University of Dayton researcher. It recaps Dayton's suspension of its Flock program after data was accessed for immigration purposes and notes other area departments' practices and records denials.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The city of Dayton suspended use of its Flock cameras \u2014 a type of ALPR that generates data that can be accessed by departments all over the country \u2014 after realizing its data was being scanned for immigration reasons in violation of city policy.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    },
    {
      "quote": "He said too often law enforcement has carte blanche access to massive amounts of data with no oversight.",
      "paragraph_idx": 27
    },
    {
      "quote": "Many local police agencies have denied or not responded to the Dayton Daily News' public record requests seeking network and internal Flock ALPR audits.",
      "paragraph_idx": 34
    }
  ],
